    destination's parent; relocating the arm, or the whole fixture root, then
    refuses the products' unchanged dependencies because the recomputed keys are NAS
    paths while the published sidecars name the originals.
    
    `logical()` is now the identity of everything this report persists or compares:
    each attempt, each run, every dependency key the products declared, the audit,
    the evidence and the rendered documents.  `stamp` and `snapshot` wrap the
    inherited ones so every check they make is unchanged and only the names they
    hand back are logical.  An attempt's published name is the one its launcher
    wrote into `train_manifest.json` as `attempt_path` -- hash-bound by the
    completion, spelled by every evaluation and every product -- and it must still
    name this very directory, which a new forgery checks by inode.
    
    exp_07 pins each checkpoint through the arm's `final` symlink
    (`ckpt/exp07/<role>/final/epoch_012.pth`, the exact string
    tools/exp07_profiles.py validates, which tools/exp07_table.py admission compares
    with the profile's arm), so the pin cannot be the attempt's name either: it is
    matched to the attempt's own output by `identical()` (samefile) and recorded at
    the attempt's path, which honours an attempt-routed pin the same way.  The
    fixture now lays the arms out as the launcher does -- `attempt_<ts>full` with
    `final` promoted to it, the approval and the profile routed through `final`, the
    evaluations naming the attempt as the eval launcher resolves it -- so the live
    routing is what the suite exercises.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

