commit 6d77a0231f3c1327cb70ccb9b66fffdd5d9eec95
Author: Yixun-Hu <yixunhu21@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Sep 18 19:54:43 2026 -0400

    exp_07 record: an archived ancestor may carry the products too
    
    `ckpt/exp07` is the natural unit to archive and it holds `results/` as well as
    the arms, so "any ancestor may be a directory symlink" has to be true of the
    products.  It was not: `make_results_md.load` identified a product by its
    resolved path while its sidecar -- and the binding report that binds it -- name
    the path it was published under, so behind a symlink a fresh `collect`,
    `check_record.py` and every regenerated document refused the product's own
    output coverage with no byte changed.  Red on all three; a product is now read
    at the name its sidecar gives it.
    
    `load_unseen` and the generators' protected-input set follow, so a regenerated
    Markdown and LaTeX name the published products byte for byte as the bound
    documents do.  Overwrite protection is unweakened and now refuses strictly more:
    the destination is compared with every protected input under BOTH spellings and
    by device and inode, so an archived input is refused under its published name
    and under the archive's.  `tools.exp07_record.write_outputs` publishes at the
    logical name and checks both spellings against the admitted inputs the same way.
    
    The fixture keeps exp_04's unseen table and binding report in their own
    directory, as the live record does (`ckpt/yaw_aug/results`): they are another
    experiment's record and archiving `ckpt/exp07` does not move them.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

