The full invocation’s two exp_06 boundary failures arose because my `--basetemp` was inside the repository: the files were correctly refused as **untracked**, while the tests expected **outside the repository**. Both passed in the corrected clone layout. The remaining failure is the known seen_simple approval guard. The full invocation itself was not zero-failure.

- **Relocation:** attempt, arm, evaluation run, and complete synthetic root—including products, audit, calibration and report—preserve unchanged-report checking and fresh collection. Regenerated Markdown, HTML and LaTeX are byte-identical and retain logical names. Changed bytes, ordinary `final` repointing and a manifest naming another attempt are refused; finding 1 identifies the remaining exception.
- **Earlier protections:** all **880 dependency mutations** have zero unexpected outcomes; **74 end-to-end mutations**, foreign-role/producer checks, **70 attempt-file/log edits**, and **75 calibration boundary checks** retain their expected behavior. Parity/XML, repeated `--evidence`, split agreement, exact coverage and terminal-state validations remain effective.
- **Live paths:** seen_simple’s `final`, manifest `attempt_path`, and all **10** evaluation checkpoint paths consistently identify `attempt_20260917T034540full`. Checkpoint inodes and recorded completion digests agree. Pins remain all-null; seen_cyl and seen_aug lack terminal receipts, so full live binding remains unavailable.
- **Training protection:** all seven files are outside the four requested closures—train **13**, launcher **22**, evaluator **22**, eval launcher **24** files. Extra launcher probe/shell files are unchanged. Finding 2 concerns the separate calibration producer closure.

